Chapter: SmpArm64Boot

 A secondary ARM64 core executes guest code, checked from inside the
 guest. Under QEMU virt the secondaries do NOT auto-enter -- they are held
 in the PSCI implementation -- so core 0's boot stub issues PSCI CPU_ON
 (conduit HVC, function id 0xC4000003) to start core 1 at an AP stub. The
 AP stub stores 1 to the marker cell at 0x60000000 and parks. That cell is
 written only by a core that ran our guest code; for these backends, until
 now, none ever had. A test showing that some computation finished proves
 nothing -- core 0 alone can do that. This reads the cell a secondary
 alone can write.

Section: Probe

  ap-marker-addr : Integer = #60000000

  poll-ap : Integer -> Integer
  poll-ap (fuel) =
   if fuel <= 0 then 0
   else let v = peek-qword ap-marker-addr 0
   in if v /= 0 then 1
   else poll-ap (fuel - 1)

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    let ran = poll-ap 100000000
    in if ran /= 0 then print-line "an ap executed guest code"
    else print-line "AP DID NOT RUN"
  end
